$image2video — image-to-video (Wan, start frame = input image)



SUMMARY

  For each image in images[], generates an MP4 using the input image as the first

  frame and the joined prompt as motion/scene guidance. New videos are appended

  to videos[]; images[] is cleared (source frames are not kept in the output).



SYNTAX

  $image2video
  $image2video(model='mega')

  $image2video(model='wan', seed=42)

  $image2video(model='wan', steps=4, guidance=1)
  $image2video(model='wan', width=832, height=480)



INPUT

  images[] — required; each link is the start frame (one video per image).

  prompts[] / instruction body — required text prompt for the model.



OUTPUT

  videos[] — one MP4 per input image ({timestamp}_{model}_i2v_{n}.mp4).

  images[] — cleared after the call.



ARGUMENTS

  model= — profile name (default mega → wan2.2-rapid-mega-aio-v12).

  width= / height= — output size in pixels (snapped to VAE/patch grid). If only one
    is set, the other follows the input image aspect ratio. If neither is set, the
    input image pixel size is used (same as Comfy at 768×1280). Optional downscale:
    WAN_I2V_MAX_AREA=399360 (480×832).

  steps= — denoising steps (default 4 for wan — matches Comfy MEGA rapid).

  frames= — output frame count (default 81). On ≤18GB GPUs, auto-capped to ≤33 unless
    WAN_I2V_NO_FRAME_CAP=1.

  tiled_vae= — 1 for tiled VAE encode/decode only (lower VRAM, slower). Not the DiT sampler.
    Aliases: vae_tiles=, tiled=. Env: WAN_I2V_TILED_VAE=1

  vram= — Comfy weight offload: low (default for tight GPUs) or novram (slowest).
    lowvram=1 is an alias. Env: WAN_I2V_VRAM=low
    DiT OOM: vram=low or novram; optional frame/resolution cap (WAN_I2V_AUTO_CAP=1).

  guidance= / cfg= — classifier-free guidance scale (default 1.0 for wan; use 1
    for Comfy-style speed, not 5).

  attn= / attention= — attention backend (default sage). Use native to force
    PyTorch SDPA only (slower but safest if sage fails).

  backend= — comfy_lib (default, ComfyUI PromptExecutor in-process) | diffusers | comfy (HTTP API)

  AH_COMFY_EXECUTOR — unset: PromptExecutor for MEGA/VACE workflows only; legacy for
  simple graphs. comfy = always PromptExecutor. legacy = always topo executor.

  seed= — RNG seed; offset per output when generating multiple videos.

  neg= / negative_prompt= — negative prompt override.



WEIGHT LAYOUT (Comfy-style AIO split, one file read)

  Single checkpoint (default):

    models/wan/wan2.2-rapid-mega-aio-v12.safetensors (default)
    models/wan/wan2.2-i2v-rapid-aio-v10.safetensors (model=wan)

  Workflow: comfy_workflows/Wan_i2v_rapid__start_image.json (same graph as WanVideo_111)

  MEGA (heavier): model=mega-nsfw (auto-picks Rapid-AIO-Mega__3_start_image.json;
    Comfy-like VRAM unload via AH_COMFY_MEMORY=1, default on for VACE).
    Loads comfy_lib/ComfyUI-WanVideoWrapper on worker start (node 34 VACE helper, etc.);
    WanVaceToVideo / WanImageToVideo still from wan_legacy_nodes when not in Wrapper.
    AH_COMFY_WAN_WRAPPER=0 disables Wrapper import (Anthill fallback for VACE node).
    On ~16GB GPUs: auto novram for MEGA; area/frame caps only if WAN_I2V_AUTO_CAP=1.
    tiled_vae=1 is optional; WAN_I2V_TILED_VAE_FULL=1 only if you need forced full VAE load.



  From that file (same prefixes as ComfyUI Load Checkpoint):

    model.diffusion_model.* — DiT (16-ch MEGA layout; VACE tensors skipped for diffusers)

    vae.*                   — Wan VAE

    text_encoders.umt5xxl.* — UMT5 text encoder



  From hub/local aux tree (configs + small files only; no transformer shards):

    tokenizer, scheduler, CLIP image encoder, image_processor

    Preferred: models/wan/i2v-base/ (Wan2.1-I2V-14B-480P-Diffusers layout)



  One-time offline configs:

    huggingface-cli download Wan-AI/Wan2.1-I2V-14B-480P-Diffusers \\

      --local-dir models/wan/i2v-base \\

      --exclude "transformer/*"



DEPENDENCIES

  uv sync --extra media   (image + image2video + comfy_lib: torchsde, scipy, einops, …)
  tools/setup_external_venvs.ps1   (creates .venvs/comfy-wan for $image2video — re-run after pyproject changes)
  uv sync --extra image2video  (ftfy, sageattention, diffusers, huggingface-hub<1.0)

  Do not install the `kernels` package — it upgrades huggingface-hub to 1.x and breaks
  transformers/diffusers on this project.



ENVIRONMENT

  WAN_I2V_BASE_DIR — local aux tree (default wan/i2v-base under models/)

  WAN_I2V_BASE_REPO — hub id when local tree absent (default Wan2.1-I2V-14B-480P)

  WAN_T2V_CONFIG_REPO — DiT config for 16-ch AIO (default Wan2.2-T2V-A14B-Diffusers)

  WAN_I2V_MAX_AREA — optional pixel cap when sizing from the input image

  WAN_I2V_ATTN — override attn= / default (sage). Example: WAN_I2V_ATTN=native

  WAN_I2V_FRAMES — override frame count (e.g. 49 for quicker runs)

  WAN_I2V_FAST_ATTN=1 — also try flash/xformers backends (optional)

  AH_IMAGE2VIDEO_WORKER=1 — warm subprocess (default; keeps Wan on GPU between jobs)
  AH_IMAGE2VIDEO_BACKEND=comfy_lib — in-process comfy_lib (default)
  AH_IMAGE2VIDEO_BACKEND=diffusers — diffusers Wan path

  AH_EMULATE_IMAGE2VIDEO=1 — placeholder MP4s, no GPU

  ComfyUI HTTP (if you prefer a running Comfy server):

    AH_IMAGE2VIDEO_BACKEND=comfy   (or backend=comfy on $image2video)

  Windows sage (for diffusers backend): tools\setup_sage_windows.ps1 after uv sync --extra media
    (triton + sageattention 2.1.1+cu128torch2.7.1; PyPI sageattention 1.0.6 needs triton
    and is slower / often falls back to _native_cudnn)



  MEGA AIO uses 16-ch patch + expand_timesteps (not hub 36-ch I2V patch). VACE weights

  in the file are not used by the diffusers path (Comfy MEGA workflows use VaceWanModel).

  Importing ComfyUI Python modules into Anthill's venv is not supported (separate env,
  folder_paths, custom nodes). Use backend=comfy to run your existing Comfy graph.



EXAMPLE

  @animate: @still -> $image2video(model='wan')

  woman running in the park

  @animate_fast: @still -> $image2video(model='wan', width=832, height=480)

  woman running in the park



PROMPT-CONSUMING

  Yes.


